{"assets":["/statement-assets/b017b719062875ac7149b017874b8f4358f698ccd0ca25487314e14d8509c6bc.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1244","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Chips"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ chips arranged in a circle, numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initially each chip has black or white color. Then $$$k$$$ iterations occur. During each iteration the chips change their colors according to the following rules. For each chip $$$i$$$, three chips are considered: chip $$$i$$$ itself and two its neighbours. If the number of white chips among these three is greater than the number of black chips among these three chips, then the chip $$$i$$$ becomes white. Otherwise, the chip $$$i$$$ becomes black. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that for each $$$i$$$ from $$$2$$$ to $$$(n - 1)$$$ two neighbouring chips have numbers $$$(i - 1)$$$ and $$$(i + 1)$$$. The neighbours for the chip $$$i = 1$$$ are $$$n$$$ and $$$2$$$. The neighbours of $$$i = n$$$ are $$$(n - 1)$$$ and $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following picture describes one iteration with $$$n = 6$$$. The chips $$$1$$$, $$$3$$$ and $$$4$$$ are initially black, and the chips $$$2$$$, $$$5$$$ and $$$6$$$ are white. After the iteration $$$2$$$, $$$3$$$ and $$$4$$$ become black, and $$$1$$$, $$$5$$$ and $$$6$$$ become white."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b017b719062875ac7149b017874b8f4358f698ccd0ca25487314e14d8509c6bc.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to determine the color of each chip after $$$k$$$ iterations."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ $$$(3 \\le n \\le 200\\,000, 1 \\le k \\le 10^{9})$$$ — the number of chips and the number of iterations, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a string consisting of $$$n$$$ characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"W"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". If the $$$i$$$-th character is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"W"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then the $$$i$$$-th chip is white initially. If the $$$i$$$-th character is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then the $$$i$$$-th chip is black initially."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a string consisting of $$$n$$$ characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"W"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". If after $$$k$$$ iterations the $$$i$$$-th chip is white, then the $$$i$$$-th character should be \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"W"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text